    {
      "category": "programme",
      "subcategory": "research",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "After decades of often heated discussions among Keynesians, monetarists, new classical and new Keynesian economists, a synthesis emerged by the 2000s, often called the new neoclassical synthesis. It integrated the rational-expectations and optimizing framework of the new classical theory with a new-Keynesian role for nominal rigidities and other market imperfections, such as imperfect information, in goods, labour, and credit markets.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source_url": "",
      "source_type": "",
      "programme_association": "",
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0011",
        "chunk_title": "New neoclassical synthesis",
        "chunk_order": 10,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "programme",
      "subcategory": "research",
      "field": "importance",
      "value": "The monetarist importance of monetary policy in stabilizing the economy and in particular controlling inflation was recognised as well as the traditional Keynesian insistence that fiscal policy could also play an influential role in affecting aggregate demand.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source_url": "",
      "source_type": "",
      "programme_association": "",
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0011",
        "chunk_title": "New neoclassical synthesis",
        "chunk_order": 10,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "programme",
      "subcategory": "research",
      "field": "applied_models",
      "value": "The synthesis led to a new class of applied models, known as dynamic stochastic general equilibrium (DSGE) models, derived from real business cycle models but extended with several new-Keynesian and other features.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source_url": "",
      "source_type": "",
      "programme_association": "",
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0011",
        "chunk_title": "New neoclassical synthesis",
        "chunk_order": 10,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "programme",
      "subcategory": "research",
      "field": "applications",
      "value": "These models proved useful and influential in the design of modern monetary policy and are now standard workhorses in most central banks.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source_url": "",
      "source_type": "",
      "programme_association": "",
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0011",
        "chunk_title": "New neoclassical synthesis",
